course: dictionary
lesson: 1907
title: Columbian: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «After 1492 ships began to link the Americas with the rest of the world» is about history, so Columbian here means to do with Christopher Columbus.
explain: Spelling is the trap. The country in South America is spelled Colombia, with an o, and its people and coffee are Colombian. The word with a u, Columbian, is for Columbus and for places called Columbia. Ask yourself: is this about a country, or about a person or place?
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. «The Columbian Exchange» means the swap of plants, animals and people after Columbus crossed the Atlantic. If your meaning fits the whole sentence, you have found it.
fact: Columbian (with a u) is an adjective: it can mean to do with Christopher Columbus, or to do with places called Columbia.
fact: Colombian (with an o) means from Colombia, the country in South America.
fact: «Pre-Columbian» means before Christopher Columbus reached the Americas, as in «pre-Columbian art».
fact: «The Columbian Exchange» means the swap of plants, animals, people and germs across the Atlantic after 1492.
fact: «British Columbian» describes someone or something from British Columbia, a province in Canada.
exercise: «After 1492 ships began to link the Americas with the rest of the world; historians call this the Columbian Exchange.» What does Columbian mean in this phrase? | *To do with Christopher Columbus | From Colombia, in South America | A kind of ship | Very old
exercise: Which spelling names the people of the country Colombia? | *Colombian | Columbus | Columbo | Columbia
exercise: «Woolly mammoths were about 3 metres tall at the shoulder; the Columbian mammoth could be over 4 metres.» What height could the Columbian mammoth reach? | *Over 4 metres | Over 10 metres | About 2 metres | About 3 metres
test: Which spelling names the country in South America? | Columbia | Columbus | *Colombia | Columbian
test: In «pre-Columbian art», what does pre-Columbian mean? | Made in a museum | *Before Christopher Columbus reached the Americas | After the year 1492 | Made by Canadians
exam: Sam wrote about coffee: «The beans were grown by Columbian farmers.» What is the mistake? | There is no mistake | *Columbian should be Colombian, from the country Colombia | Beans should be spelled beens | Farmers should be spelled with an e
